+The concurrency mechanism belongs to record-store, not this HLD. It is whole-visit revisions: each accepted submission is stored as a complete revision naming the revision it was edited from. A submission naming the visit's current revision advances the visit, but only while the visit has no unresolved review work; a submission naming any other revision of the visit is held as a competing revision for coordinator review, and a submission naming a revision the visit does not hold is rejected. A visit with unresolved review work is held out of the partner CSV until a coordinator resolves it. Tablet-sync and review-export are written against that contract, which fixes the submission metadata, the shape of review work, and which record states can enter an export.
 
 ## Tenets
 
 - Do not silently discard a submitted edit.
+- Prefer an explicit coordinator over an automated combination of scientifically related observations.
 - Let field workers continue collecting observations without connectivity.
 - Keep the path from a submitted observation to an exported value inspectable.
 - Prefer workflows two coordinators can operate without a dedicated systems administrator.
