+- [ ] **REC-047**: When the system applies the checks for a submission, the system SHALL apply them in the order authentication, idempotency, payload validation, and concurrency outcome, and SHALL report the first applicable reason for a rejected submission.
+- [ ] **REC-048**: When a caller lacks the coordinator role, the system SHALL refuse the request before looking up the requested visit.
+- [ ] **REC-049**: When a visit has an open review round, the system SHALL not open a second review round for that visit, and SHALL store any further competing revision for that visit in the round already open.
+- [ ] **REC-050**: When the system stores a revision, the system SHALL stamp the revision's server receipt time when the submission reaches the server and SHALL assign the revision's sequence number when the revision is stored.
+- [ ] **REC-051**: When a coordinator submits a revision naming the visit's current revision as its base while the visit has an open review round, the system SHALL store that revision as a competing revision in the open round and SHALL resolve it by the same rule as any other competing revision.
+- [ ] **REC-052**: When a submitted payload names a plot that the site catalog knows and has archived, the system SHALL accept the submission.
+- [ ] **REC-053**: When the system validates a submitted plot identifier, the system SHALL validate it against the site's authoritative catalog rather than against a snapshot cached on a tablet.
+- [ ] **REC-054**: When a caller retrieves a visit's current state, the system SHALL return whether the visit is eligible for the partner CSV.
